<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105981" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύρβη</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>disorder, confusion, tumult,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύρβην παρέχειν τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Fract.</u>
					22
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν τύρβην ἐν ᾗ ζῶμεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					15.130
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.2.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.67.3
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ποιητικὴ τ.</span> the poetic
				<i>rout,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				228
			</span></i>; so of a <i>Bacchic festival and its dance,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				2.24.6
			</span></i>: hence, acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπόλαυσις</span>
			, <i>revelry.</i> [Oxyt. in some codd. of <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i> l.c.; the form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύρβη</span> is
			cited by <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				871.60
			</span></i>.] (Cf. Lat. <i>turba,</i> O Norse <i>pyrpask</i> 'crowd
			together'.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
